## Rust standard library in native binaries

The Fcitx5 binary statically links the build toolchain's Rust standard library.
Native archives and packages include its COPYRIGHT-library.html, license texts
and compiler identity under rust-stdlib beside the project license. These are
copied from the actual toolchain at build time; missing notices fail the build.
The standard library is Apache-2.0 OR MIT with component exceptions described
in that copyright file, including BSD-2-Clause and Unicode-3.0 material. Original
Jong code remains MIT. Bundled license texts describe their respective material,
not a relicensing of Jong. Dynamic Fcitx5 and C/C++ runtime dependencies remain
distribution packages with their own notices.

